  Quote of the Week:

  Imperial Motto of Frederick III (1415-1493), Holy Roman Emperor and ruler 
of Austria:
  "The whole world is subject to Austria"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the advent of the spring season, Bradipo I prepared to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He could not cast Resurrection on Alexius because 
Alexius was still alive.  Instead, Bradipo I discovered nothing worthy of 
note in his sagely experiments.
  Windy spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  Bradipo I cruised 
over to Kiska.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
marched on the Mountain province of Transylvania, a land garrisoned by the 
forces of Bradipo I.  Rainulf (#25)'s forces encountered little resistance 
in Transylvania and Rainulf there established our reign.  Rainulf leads 
approximately 3 Garrison.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
marched on the Jungle province of Mongu, a land garrisoned by the forces of 
Bradipo I.  Tlazolteotl (#88) commanded the invading armies.  The defenders 
were commanded by the provincial garrison commander.  The armies were drawn 
up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Mongu (0305):

  256th     106th      75th   
 Dragons   Dragons   Dragons  
