  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with her warriors was Tlazolteotl.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of Bradipo I.
  Tlazolteotl had conducted a long flanking march to try to catch the acting 
commander off guard.  But the ruse failed, and its only effect was to 
demoralize Tlazolteotl's troops considerably.  On the other hand tactical 
superiority was clearly assured by Tlazolteotl's powerful tactical mind.
  Bradipo I's soldiers were prepared to struggle desperately for their 
fatherland.
  Out on the right outside flank, the Crack 223rd Phalanx faced the 4th 
Garrison.  The 256th Dragons swooped down on the 4th Garrison and attacked 
without mercy.  The 223rd Phalanx fought the 4th Garrison and smashed them 
like rotten oranges.
  In the interior lines, the Crack 222nd Phalanx faced the 41st Legion.  The 
unwieldy formation of the 222nd Phalanx was severely shaken by the flexible 
Legionnaires.  The 106th Dragons swooped down on the 41st Legion and 
attacked them.
  Tlazolteotl maneuvered the 106th Dragons to the front line, as a strategem 
for a better match-up.  Here, the soldiers of the 41st Legion got lost in a 
patch of fog, which whittled down their forces a little.  The 106th Dragons 
fought with the 41st Legion and aggressively knifed into them.
  Out on the left outside wing, the Elite 139th Phalanx faced the 29th 
Garrison.  The 75th Dragons swooped down on the 29th Garrison and attacked 
them.  The 139th Phalanx fought with the 29th Garrison and overpowered them 
with their thundering charge.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Tlazolteotl as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 223rd Phalanx destroyed the 4th Garrison. 
The 139th Phalanx slew the 29th Garrison almost to a man.  The 256th Dragons 
pursued the enemy and annihilated the 41st Legion.
  Tlazolteotl's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered Mongu.  
The acting commander pulled back to Macondo with its command.
  In late summer, Bradipo I cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 265th 
Skeletal Axemen arose from the graves of the dead!
  With the coming of the fall season Bradipo I tried a Tornado spell, but 
bungled it.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Bradipo I announced a plea for 
recruits in Kiska and was able to enlist the 141st Eagles to fight for 
Bradipo I.  Bradipo I could not recruit more Eagles in Kiska because the 
provincial maximum had already been recruited.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Bradipo I for this year.


  Bradipo I treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Bradipo I 
treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Bradipo I treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Bradipo I treated with 
his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Circe (#8).  
Bradipo I treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Tilden (#47) grew tired of the scenery in Abu Matariq and departed for Bam 
Yanga.


  Here is the financial report for Bradipo I's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 26 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 141st Eagles trained well and improved in quality.  7 gold was 
expended to maintain our armies.  Bradipo I was left with 110 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Adele
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  I announced a call for volunteers in Mongu and 
was able to form the 4th Garrison, the 29th Garrison and the 41st Legion to 
fight for the provincial garrison commander.  I could find no soldiers in 
Mongu for the requested Elephants troops.
  With the advent of the early summer season I moved into Big Sky.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer came.  I strengthened 
my forces in Big Sky with the 31st Legion, the 76th Eagles, the 207th Eagles 
and the 289th Phalanx.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Big Sky, a 
Mountain area owned by Bradipo I.  Tlazolteotl (#88) commanded the invading 
armies.  The defending forces were led by me.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Big Sky (0306):

