  DEFENDING ARMY

  Tlazolteotl stood ready at the head of her thousands.  I commanded a host 
of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  Tlazolteotl strode forward and challenged me to personal combat.  I 
refused to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by me were disappointed by my cowardice.  They 
marched on, though with shaken confidence.  Tlazolteotl allowed a prisoner 
to overhear that reinforcements would soon come to augment her forces, then 
gave him a chance to escape.  The prisoner reported the grim news to me, and 
I deployed my forces with excessive caution.  Further, tactical supremacy 
was guaranteed by Tlazolteotl's powerful tactical mind.
  The Eagles I commanded were ineffective because of their poor relations 
with me.
  Out on the right outside flank, the Elite 139th Phalanx were arrayed 
against the Crack 31st Legion.  The unwieldy mass of the 139th Phalanx was 
tested by the flexible Legionnaires.  The 75th Dragons soared over the 31st 
Legion and attacked them.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 75th Dragons to the fore, as a strategem for a 
superior match-up.  The 75th Dragons fought with the 31st Legion and smashed 
them like rotten tomatoes.
  In the interior front, the Crack 223rd Phalanx were arrayed against the 
76th Eagles, who sang their heroic ballads, infused with a spirit of holy, 
fanatical fury by their exalted King.  The 256th Dragons soared over the 
76th Eagles and attacked them.  The 223rd Phalanx fought the 76th Eagles and 
cut them down like weeds.
  Out on the left flank, the Crack 222nd Phalanx were arrayed against the 
Crack 289th Phalanx.  The 106th Dragons swooped down on the 207th Eagles and 
attacked without mercy.  The 207th Eagles soared over the 106th Dragons and 
attacked them.  The 222nd Phalanx battled with the 289th Phalanx and smashed 
their skulls as if they were eggshells.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Tlazolteotl as they 
broke through the lines at a critical moment.  The 75th Dragons scattered 
the 31st Legion in all directions.  The 222nd Phalanx annihilated the 289th 
Phalanx.  The 106th Dragons slew the 207th Eagles almost to a man.
  Big Sky was overrun by Tlazolteotl's men in a hard-fought campaign.  The 
76th Eagles were unable to escape and were disbanded into the population.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to fall.  I failed in my ineffectual 
attempt to cast a Plague spell.
  With the coming of the early winter season I rode into Rosehaven.  East of 
here is the Crab Sea (#507), a prosperous Sea area ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where Whales dwell.  If need be, they can 
call on a host of Whales to defend their province.  Looking to the southeast,
one can see a Desert area, which is known as the Hammerhead Sea (#408).  It 
is populated by no races and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules there.

  Thy humble servant,   Adele


From: Indra
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my 
natural ability.  I invented nothing worthy of note in my sagely 
experiments.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I rehearsed and practiced my 
Sageness and improved noticeably.
  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Sageness.  At levels 5 
and up, there is not necessarily an increase in the chance to invent 
something.  Instead, the Sage attracts a company of philosphers and builds a 
University in his province of birth.  Your characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  I invented nothing in my sagely researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season I tried to practice my Sageness, 
but the task was beyond my natural ability.  I discovered nothing valuable 
in my sagely researches.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I discovered 
nothing in my sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early winter season I tried to improve my Sageness, 
but the task seemed beyond my ability.  My efforts improved my aptitude in 
Sageness.  I invented nothing valuable in my sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Indra


